I don't think jetpack will have much chance of running without -DBLIT;
here is mail I sent to Mark:

------
Well, you asked me to build it without BLIT (on the HP Snake).  It doesn't
work because of this in erase.c:

	#define MAXOBJECTS 6+MAXLINES+MAXFIREBALLS+MAXSWEEPERS+MAXFUELPODS+MAXGUARDS+MAXHIGHSCORES/5

	/*      Structure for eraseable zones that minimize flicker
	*/
	struct zone {
		int     type, num;
		int     x, y, w, h;
		int     numtouch;
		int     touch[MAXOBJECTS];
		int     erased, drawn;
	};

	int                     numzones;
	struct zone     zones[MAXOBJECTS];

MAXOBJECTS is 6+100*100*2+100+100+40+40+50+40+25/5 == 20381, and the above
calls for 20381 struct zones, each containing 20381 ints.  THIS IS HUGE:

	coltsfoot:jetpack 626 j$ ./jetpack
	exec(2): data extends beyond end of a.out
	./jetpack: Bad address.
	coltsfoot:jetpack 627 j$ size !$
	size ./jetpack
	56906 + 38448 + 1662646956 = 1662742310

I think you need to consider a sparse array (or dropping those dimmensions!).

John


